WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
Across England, 54 per cent of new
residential addresses were on land that had

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.570
been built on before.

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.630
And London had the highest share of all.

4
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.910
That means sites like
old factories and docks.

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.070
Yet open farmland lies at the city's edge.

6
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.790
So why not just build
on the fields around it?

7
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.110
Is old land simply cheaper?

8
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.610
In this mission, you'll sort building
land into brownfield and greenfield,

9
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.570
and weigh the case for each.

10
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.530
Then you'll test London's
choice against the evidence,

11
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.250
and decide which kind of
site makes the stronger case.

12
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.390
Your mission: explain why London builds
most of its new homes on old land,

13
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.170
not on the fields around it.
